      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Institutional mortality refers to deaths that occur while patients are admitted in hospitals and other inpatient \nfacilities.\nIn many countries, most deaths occur outside of health facilities, because of access challenges such as distance \nand lack of transport, as well as cultural, legal, security and financial issues. Civil registration and vital statistics \n(CRVS) systems are the official source of mortality information in a country or an administrative unit such as a \ndistrict. However, these systems are under-developed in many contexts and other than estimates derived from \npopulation-bas",
